sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch11-04> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "In a scorpioid cyme, where each shoot arises from the last on the same side at an equal angle and successive shoots diminish in length in a constant ratio, the shoots are tangents to a true logarithmic spiral; in the helicoid cyme the same spiral is present but hidden by a superimposed twist.";
    dc:type "mathematical-law";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The scorpioid cyme traces a true logarithmic spiral";
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "successive shoots l_{n+1} = q\\,l_n at equal angles are tangents to r = a e^{\\theta\\cot\\alpha}";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "D’Arcy Wentworth Thompson, On Growth and Form (1st ed., Cambridge: Cambridge University Press, 1917), Chapter XI, “The Logarithmic Spiral”; topic “Cymose inflorescences”. Scope: scorpioid and helicoid (cymose) inflorescences, e.g. borage"
}
